# General Coding Standards (gfa-health-hms)

## Stack

- Vite + React 18 + TypeScript
- React Router, TanStack Query, React Hook Form + Zod
- shadcn/ui + Tailwind
- Vitest (unit) and Playwright (e2e)

## TypeScript

- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions and mapped types.
- Avoid `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow with type guards.
- Colocate feature types near the module that owns them.

## React

- Functional components and hooks only.
- Put shared UI in `src/components/`; pages in `src/pages/`.
- Reuse shadcn primitives from `src/components/ui/`.
- Prefer data access via `src/data-access/` hooks and local fixtures over ad-hoc network calls.
- This demo has **no backend** — do not wire `VITE_USE_API=true`.

## Forms & Validation

- Use React Hook Form with Zod resolvers for non-trivial forms.
- Surface validation errors next to fields; use `sonner` / existing notify helpers for async feedback.

## Env & Secrets

- Read env only through `src/lib/env.ts` (offline demo lock).
- Never commit real API URLs/tokens for production backends.

## Design

- Match established layout and the GFA royal-blue / mint palette.
